1
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:41,068
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,068 --> 00:02:45,068
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,068 --> 00:02:52,068
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,068 --> 00:02:58,068
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,068 --> 00:03:09,068
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,068 --> 00:03:13,068
I will be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,068 --> 00:03:25,068
In the two years that have passed since the War of the Best in Marineford, the Straw Hat Pirates underwent special training before returning to the Sabaody Archipelago.

8
00:03:25,068 --> 00:03:32,068
Now, in order to progress to the New World, Luffy and his crew have arrived at Fishman Island, thousands of feet below sea level.

9
00:03:32,068 --> 00:03:39,068
However, they were attacked by the new Fishman Pirates, causing them to become separated yet again.

10
00:03:39,068 --> 00:03:45,068
In this time of need, Mermaids managed to rescue some of the crew and bring them safely to Kami's home.

11
00:03:48,068 --> 00:03:51,068
Now, what did I do?

12
00:03:51,068 --> 00:03:54,068
We don't have time! Guys, this is serious!

13
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:59,068
Please, I'm begging you! Whatever it takes! I can't let my friend die!

14
00:03:59,068 --> 00:04:06,068
The Fishman Island will be annihilated? Charlie's prophecy!

15
00:04:06,068 --> 00:04:13,068
We need help! My friend is dying! Can anyone give him blood?

16
00:04:13,068 --> 00:04:17,068
Human or Fishman, SRH- is his type!

17
00:04:17,068 --> 00:04:20,068
He doesn't have much time! Please, we're begging you!

18
00:04:20,068 --> 00:04:22,068
Help him!

19
00:04:30,068 --> 00:04:36,068
Poor thing. I'm sorry. This is a bad place for a human to get a blood transfusion.

20
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:40,068
But, I'm sure Luffy Chin and your friends will figure something out.

21
00:04:40,068 --> 00:04:50,068
Damn it! No matter who we ask, there isn't anyone here who will give him blood! Come on!

22
00:04:50,068 --> 00:04:53,068
I refuse to give up! Sanji's counting on us!

23
00:04:53,068 --> 00:04:55,068
There's gotta be somebody!

24
00:04:58,068 --> 00:05:03,068
Oh, right! Luffy! I found some humans here!

25
00:05:03,068 --> 00:05:15,068
Hey, that barrel over there is the one that drifted in with all Kami's friends, right?

26
00:05:15,068 --> 00:05:18,068
What's in it? Maybe... treasure?

27
00:05:18,068 --> 00:05:19,068
Uh...

28
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:22,068
I don't know. It's sealed pretty tightly, so it's gotta be important.

29
00:05:23,068 --> 00:05:26,068
Yeah? I think we should open it.

30
00:05:26,068 --> 00:05:28,068
Me too. What if it needs to go in the fridge?

31
00:05:30,068 --> 00:05:31,068
Good point.

32
00:05:31,068 --> 00:05:34,068
Wow. Talk about well prepared.

33
00:05:34,068 --> 00:05:35,068
Way to go!

34
00:05:46,068 --> 00:05:48,068
Hey, Sanji! Are you awake?

35
00:05:48,068 --> 00:05:49,068
Talk to us!

36
00:05:51,068 --> 00:05:52,068
Where am I?

37
00:05:54,068 --> 00:05:55,068
You pulled through!

38
00:05:56,068 --> 00:05:59,068
We're safe in a town right by the harbor. I was scared.

39
00:05:59,068 --> 00:06:02,068
You almost lost all the blood in your body.

40
00:06:02,068 --> 00:06:07,068
I was starting to think we'd never find you a donor. That was a real close call.

41
00:06:08,068 --> 00:06:09,068
That so? Wow.

42
00:06:12,068 --> 00:06:14,068
What in the hell happened... to me?

43
00:06:15,068 --> 00:06:18,068
You shouldn't be sitting up so quickly. You need to rest.

44
00:06:18,068 --> 00:06:27,068
I just don't get it. I mean, the fish could have given blood. But no, instead we had to run all over town looking for another human. Which took forever.

45
00:06:27,068 --> 00:06:30,068
I know, right? I was starting to lose hope there.

46
00:06:30,068 --> 00:06:41,068
I'm sorry. I appreciate what you did, though. But I just don't remember much. Why'd this happen? Where was I and what was I doing? When I think about it, it's all a big blip.

47
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:44,068
Ah! No! Let it go already!

48
00:06:45,068 --> 00:06:47,068
If you try to force the memories, you could relapse!

49
00:06:48,068 --> 00:06:55,068
Oh, yeah. I almost forgot, Sanji. You haven't met your donors. So here, say hi. And also thank you.

50
00:06:55,068 --> 00:07:04,068
Wait. Could my savior have been... a dainty girl?

51
00:07:08,068 --> 00:07:15,068
Don't worry. We're only human. After all, if we don't look out for each other, who will?

52
00:07:15,068 --> 00:07:25,068
Don't worry, babe. If you want, we can give you more.

53
00:07:36,068 --> 00:07:38,068
Looks like he's back to his old self.

54
00:07:40,068 --> 00:07:42,068
That's not exactly gratitude.

55
00:07:43,068 --> 00:07:44,068
Luffy?

56
00:07:45,068 --> 00:07:47,068
Can I see the cut on your arm for a second, please?

57
00:07:47,068 --> 00:07:48,068
Huh?

58
00:07:52,068 --> 00:07:53,068
It's positive.

59
00:07:54,068 --> 00:07:57,068
Thought so. Luffy, that wound's poisonous.

60
00:07:58,068 --> 00:08:01,068
Oh, wow. Really? That must have been the sting I felt earlier.

61
00:08:02,068 --> 00:08:03,068
One of the fish men got me.

62
00:08:04,068 --> 00:08:07,068
You don't seem poisoned. You feeling okay?

63
00:08:08,068 --> 00:08:09,068
Yeah.

64
00:08:09,068 --> 00:08:10,068
Either way, we should be careful.

65
00:08:11,068 --> 00:08:14,068
This stuff's probably deadly. You sure you're all right?

66
00:08:14,068 --> 00:08:15,068
Yep.

67
00:08:15,068 --> 00:08:22,068
Wow. So weird. It sounds crazy. But you must have somehow developed an antibody to fight against this kind of stuff.

68
00:08:23,068 --> 00:08:26,068
Tell me, have you ever experienced a poisoning like this in the past?

69
00:08:26,068 --> 00:08:27,068
Let's see.

70
00:08:27,068 --> 00:08:35,068
Yeah. Back when I was at Impel Down, I almost got killed that way.

71
00:08:35,068 --> 00:08:36,068
That is not funny at all.

72
00:08:36,068 --> 00:08:52,068
Yeah, it is. I bet it was that octopus swordsman. I mean, he blocked my punch, so he's gotta be strong. No prob. Next time, I'll be ready.

73
00:08:52,068 --> 00:08:53,068
Huh?

74
00:08:53,068 --> 00:09:19,068
They're so loud. I think that came from by that cove. Don't care. I've got bigger problems. These guys are messed up real bad. And what's worse, Straw Hat got poisoned too. I'm dead if he dies.

75
00:09:19,068 --> 00:09:26,068
I'm positive I heard their screams come from here. Ishili! Where are you?

76
00:09:27,068 --> 00:09:31,068
This is where I saw them last. But where in the world could they have gone?

77
00:09:31,068 --> 00:09:35,068
Did anyone else hear them say something about opening up a barrel?

78
00:09:39,068 --> 00:09:43,068
Hey, Luffy-chin, Usopp-chin, come here. There's someone I'd like you to meet.

79
00:09:43,068 --> 00:09:44,068
Huh?

80
00:09:44,068 --> 00:09:53,068
She's the owner of this place. She okayed Sanji resting here. The Madam Charlie.

81
00:09:53,068 --> 00:09:55,068
Cool. Thanks and stuff.

82
00:09:55,068 --> 00:09:59,068
Has the blonde boy's condition improved at all?

83
00:09:59,068 --> 00:10:11,068
Yep. But it's best he doesn't meet you because you're so beautiful. Right? That would be bad. Also, we probably shouldn't tell him he's in the back of the mermaid cafe. Not if we want him to get well.

84
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:13,068
Why keep it a secret?

85
00:10:13,068 --> 00:10:18,068
Cuz doctor's orders. Chakra's pretty sure that if Sanji-chin finds out, he's gonna have a bad relapse.

86
00:10:18,068 --> 00:10:21,068
What a strange prognosis.

87
00:10:21,068 --> 00:10:24,068
Hey, big lady! Fish lady!

88
00:10:24,068 --> 00:10:27,068
Wow, that was rude. Come on.

89
00:10:27,068 --> 00:10:28,068
Tell me what this is.

90
00:10:28,068 --> 00:10:29,068
It's beautiful.

91
00:10:29,068 --> 00:10:32,068
It's also not on the list of things you're allowed to touch.

92
00:10:32,068 --> 00:10:42,068
Huh? Oh, that? You're looking at Madam Charlie's crystal ball. With it, she can see the future. Her precognitive visions are why she's famous.

93
00:10:42,068 --> 00:10:45,068
Well, it used to be. Not anymore.

94
00:10:45,068 --> 00:10:46,068
Huh?

95
00:10:46,068 --> 00:10:53,068
The future isn't ours to know, right?

96
00:10:53,068 --> 00:10:54,068
Huh?

97
00:10:54,068 --> 00:10:58,068
Sounds rough. Oh, by the way, how do mermaids take a dump?

98
00:10:58,068 --> 00:11:01,068
We are not talking about mermaid poop again!

99
00:11:01,068 --> 00:11:03,068
Don't you have any class?

100
00:11:03,068 --> 00:11:05,068
Guys, apologize! Quickly!

101
00:11:06,068 --> 00:11:07,068
Sorry.

102
00:11:07,068 --> 00:11:14,068
Why don't you take the rest of the day off, Kami? I think your friends would appreciate a tour of the island.

103
00:11:14,068 --> 00:11:16,068
Really? You sure?

104
00:11:16,068 --> 00:11:20,068
It's fine. You deserve it, seeing as you're always working so hard.

105
00:11:20,068 --> 00:11:27,068
Besides, business has been slow with human guests so uncommon these days. So we have to be extra good hosts.

106
00:11:27,068 --> 00:11:32,068
The girls from the cove should show up soon. Then we'll have more hands around here than a starfish.

107
00:11:32,068 --> 00:11:34,068
More than... starfish?

108
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:39,068
Oh, that's right! Crap! I should've already delivered Papa Goose clams by now!

109
00:11:39,068 --> 00:11:42,068
Wow. I have no idea what's going on.

110
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:45,068
I bet he's getting mad waiting for his food.

111
00:11:45,068 --> 00:11:52,068
Not quite. He's enjoying the cafe. An old friend of his suddenly came into town, and they've been living it up since he arrived.

112
00:11:52,068 --> 00:11:53,068
Wait. He's here?

113
00:11:53,068 --> 00:11:55,068
Well, that makes things easy.

114
00:12:01,068 --> 00:12:06,068
I didn't want to bring this up in front of her, but Madam told me a lot of stories from when she was little.

115
00:12:06,068 --> 00:12:11,068
She said in those days human pirates came to the island all the time.

116
00:12:11,068 --> 00:12:16,068
But that was quite a while ago. About a year before the Great Pirate Era began.

117
00:12:18,068 --> 00:12:25,068
It's hard for her to talk about things sometimes, especially when she foresees bad stuff like the war at Marineford and Whitebeard's death.

118
00:12:25,068 --> 00:12:26,068
What?!

119
00:12:26,068 --> 00:12:30,068
Can you imagine knowing something horrible will happen that you can't stop?

120
00:12:30,068 --> 00:12:32,068
That must be terrifying!

121
00:12:32,068 --> 00:12:33,068
Hey, where's Chopper?

122
00:12:33,068 --> 00:12:36,068
Oh, he said he was gonna hang out here and look after Sanji.

123
00:12:36,068 --> 00:12:38,068
Come on, you two! Hurry up!

124
00:12:38,068 --> 00:12:39,068
Kay!

125
00:12:39,068 --> 00:12:49,068
Right now we're on what's considered Coral Hill's main street. And that is the primary entrance to the Mermaid Cafe!

126
00:12:50,068 --> 00:12:55,068
Man, thought I was gonna starve to death.

127
00:12:55,068 --> 00:12:57,068
They might only serve snacks.

128
00:12:57,068 --> 00:13:00,068
No, you're good. We've got cakes and sea fruit too!

129
00:13:00,068 --> 00:13:01,068
And meat?

130
00:13:02,068 --> 00:13:10,068
Uh, no. We merfolk don't really eat meat and fish. But we have wakame brulee, mozuku tarts, kelp souffle...

131
00:13:10,068 --> 00:13:12,068
You call that food?

132
00:13:12,068 --> 00:13:14,068
Wait! We do have some meat!

133
00:13:15,068 --> 00:13:18,068
From shellfish! Scallop sandwiches, plant pizza, and...

134
00:13:18,068 --> 00:13:21,068
Those give me the bad name! Stop talking!

135
00:13:21,068 --> 00:13:25,068
Whoa! Okay, be cool. Let's just go inside.

136
00:13:25,068 --> 00:13:27,068
Yeah, let's all go find Papagu.

137
00:13:27,068 --> 00:13:30,068
Shellfish! What the hell kind of crab is that?!

138
00:13:30,068 --> 00:13:31,068
Thank you very much!

139
00:13:31,068 --> 00:13:32,068
Yeah!

140
00:13:34,068 --> 00:13:36,068
Time to give the dogfish a bone.

141
00:13:36,068 --> 00:13:38,068
Gotta love the fins, huh?

142
00:13:51,068 --> 00:13:54,068
Oh, wow! It's Brooke!

143
00:13:54,068 --> 00:13:55,068
Hooray!

144
00:13:55,068 --> 00:13:56,068
Huh?

145
00:13:56,068 --> 00:13:57,068
Luffy and Usopp?

146
00:13:57,068 --> 00:14:00,068
And Kami, you've become such a lovely young lady!

147
00:14:00,068 --> 00:14:01,068
Now, may I please see your panties?

148
00:14:01,068 --> 00:14:02,068
Mermaids don't wear those!

149
00:14:02,068 --> 00:14:03,068
Hey, guys!

150
00:14:03,068 --> 00:14:05,068
You have no idea how much I've missed you!

151
00:14:05,068 --> 00:14:06,068
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

152
00:14:06,068 --> 00:14:08,068
Hey, Papagu! Sorry it's been so long!

153
00:14:08,068 --> 00:14:10,068
I guess that makes you Papagu's old friend we heard about!

154
00:14:10,068 --> 00:14:11,068
Yes, though...

155
00:14:11,068 --> 00:14:12,068
I've missed you!

156
00:14:12,068 --> 00:14:13,068
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

157
00:14:13,068 --> 00:14:15,068
Hey, Papagu! Sorry it's been so long!

158
00:14:15,068 --> 00:14:18,068
I guess that makes you Papagu's old friend we heard about!

159
00:14:18,068 --> 00:14:20,068
Yes, though...

160
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:23,068
I wish the reunion had better circumstances,

161
00:14:23,068 --> 00:14:26,068
because without him I'd be sunk!

162
00:14:26,068 --> 00:14:28,068
Don't let the laugh fool you!

163
00:14:28,068 --> 00:14:29,068
He means that literally!

164
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:31,068
There I was, hard at work by the cove,

165
00:14:31,068 --> 00:14:33,068
finalizing a design idea I had,

166
00:14:33,068 --> 00:14:34,068
when all of a sudden,

167
00:14:34,068 --> 00:14:37,068
a pile of bones went drifting by on a log!

168
00:14:37,068 --> 00:14:38,068
Huh?

169
00:14:39,068 --> 00:14:41,068
Bone Daddy!

170
00:14:43,068 --> 00:14:45,068
Come see us again, K?

171
00:14:45,068 --> 00:14:48,068
I had a great time, Soul King!

172
00:14:48,068 --> 00:14:52,068
I'll be back, lovely ladies!

173
00:14:52,068 --> 00:14:54,068
Lots of bones to go around!

174
00:14:54,068 --> 00:14:55,068
What?!

175
00:14:55,068 --> 00:14:56,068
Oh, I've gone limp!

176
00:14:56,068 --> 00:15:00,068
No, I haven't!

177
00:15:00,068 --> 00:15:03,068
Skeletons are always rigid!

178
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,068
Good thing I'm already dead,

179
00:15:05,068 --> 00:15:08,068
or I would probably die of embarrassment right now!

180
00:15:08,068 --> 00:15:09,068
Oh, you!

181
00:15:09,068 --> 00:15:12,068
This cafe's really put Brooke in rare form!

182
00:15:12,068 --> 00:15:15,068
Yeah, whatever's going on inside must be awesome!

183
00:15:15,068 --> 00:15:16,068
Hold up there, boss!

184
00:15:16,068 --> 00:15:17,068
Huh?

185
00:15:17,068 --> 00:15:19,068
What are you in such a hurry for?

186
00:15:19,068 --> 00:15:21,068
I know you're interested in the cafe,

187
00:15:21,068 --> 00:15:22,068
and I get that,

188
00:15:22,068 --> 00:15:24,068
but it's not like it's going anywhere!

189
00:15:24,068 --> 00:15:26,068
Let's come back when you have your whole crew!

190
00:15:26,068 --> 00:15:29,068
Bone Daddy and I were just about to head back to my place!

191
00:15:29,068 --> 00:15:31,068
Why don't you guys come with us?

192
00:15:31,068 --> 00:15:33,068
If you do,

193
00:15:33,068 --> 00:15:35,068
you can eat all the Sea King meat you want!

194
00:15:35,068 --> 00:15:37,068
Did you say meat?!

195
00:15:37,068 --> 00:15:38,068
Yeah, I did!

196
00:15:38,068 --> 00:15:41,068
I'm a wild animal, you feel me?

197
00:15:41,068 --> 00:15:43,068
It's not like I eat boring shellfish!

198
00:15:43,068 --> 00:15:45,068
I need food with a little more bite!

199
00:15:45,068 --> 00:15:47,068
Sea Monster Exclusive Diet!

200
00:15:47,068 --> 00:15:48,068
Oh!

201
00:15:48,068 --> 00:15:49,068
By the way,

202
00:15:49,068 --> 00:15:50,068
I brought your order of clams!

203
00:15:50,068 --> 00:15:51,068
Sweet!

204
00:15:51,068 --> 00:15:53,068
My favorite treat is finally here!

205
00:15:53,068 --> 00:15:54,068
Ha!

206
00:15:54,068 --> 00:15:55,068
Oh!

207
00:15:55,068 --> 00:15:56,068
So much for your diet!

208
00:15:56,068 --> 00:15:57,068
Oh, man!

209
00:16:02,068 --> 00:16:04,068
Beautiful mermaid!

210
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:05,068
Yes!

211
00:16:05,068 --> 00:16:06,068
Ah!

212
00:16:06,068 --> 00:16:07,068
Lovely mermaids!

213
00:16:07,068 --> 00:16:08,068
So sweet!

214
00:16:08,068 --> 00:16:09,068
You okay, hun?!

215
00:16:09,068 --> 00:16:10,068
Ah!

216
00:16:10,068 --> 00:16:11,068
Lovely mermaids!

217
00:16:11,068 --> 00:16:12,068
So sweet!

218
00:16:12,068 --> 00:16:13,068
You okay, hun?!

219
00:16:13,068 --> 00:16:14,068
Ah!

220
00:16:14,068 --> 00:16:15,068
Lovely!

221
00:16:15,068 --> 00:16:16,068
This sucks!

222
00:16:16,068 --> 00:16:17,068
I hope they're having better luck!

223
00:16:17,068 --> 00:16:18,068
Wonderful!

224
00:16:18,068 --> 00:16:19,068
Ah!

225
00:16:19,068 --> 00:16:20,068
Sweet spelling!

226
00:16:20,068 --> 00:16:22,068
Look, merfolk are the only ones who don't eat meat!

227
00:16:22,068 --> 00:16:23,068
Fishmen eat the stuff all the time!

228
00:16:23,068 --> 00:16:24,068
So it's not like you can't get it here!

229
00:16:24,068 --> 00:16:25,068
It's just not as common!

230
00:16:25,068 --> 00:16:26,068
Yes!

231
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:27,068
That's great!

232
00:16:27,068 --> 00:16:29,068
Man, it's about time one of them showed up!

233
00:16:29,068 --> 00:16:30,068
Hey, taxi!

234
00:16:30,068 --> 00:16:31,068
Hey, wait a minute!

235
00:16:31,068 --> 00:16:32,068
Oh!

236
00:16:32,068 --> 00:16:33,068
Vander Decken thought so!

237
00:16:33,068 --> 00:16:35,068
But why is there a wanted poster for a ghost?

238
00:16:35,068 --> 00:16:36,068
Yeah!

239
00:16:36,068 --> 00:16:38,068
Wasn't this guy on the haunted ship we saw?

240
00:16:38,068 --> 00:16:39,068
You saw him?

241
00:16:39,068 --> 00:16:40,068
For real?

242
00:16:40,068 --> 00:16:41,068
Uh-huh!

243
00:16:41,068 --> 00:16:42,068
No way!

244
00:16:42,068 --> 00:16:43,068
Whoa!

245
00:16:43,068 --> 00:16:44,068
Our nation's been looking for him for years now!

246
00:16:44,068 --> 00:16:46,068
The dude's a pirate and a no-good undersea thief!

247
00:16:46,068 --> 00:16:47,068
I'll tell you all about it on the trip!

248
00:16:47,068 --> 00:16:48,068
Let's load up!

249
00:16:48,068 --> 00:16:49,068
And go!

250
00:16:49,068 --> 00:16:50,068
Let's load up!

251
00:16:50,068 --> 00:16:51,068
Hey, taxi!

252
00:16:51,068 --> 00:16:52,068
Hey, taxi!

253
00:16:52,068 --> 00:16:53,068
Hey, wait a minute!

254
00:16:53,068 --> 00:16:54,068
Wait a minute!

255
00:16:54,068 --> 00:16:55,068
Oh!

256
00:16:55,068 --> 00:16:56,068
Vander Decken thought so!

257
00:16:56,068 --> 00:16:58,068
But why is there a wanted poster for a ghost?

258
00:16:58,068 --> 00:16:59,068
Yeah!

259
00:16:59,068 --> 00:17:01,068
Wasn't this guy on the haunted ship we saw?

260
00:17:01,068 --> 00:17:02,068
You saw him?

261
00:17:02,068 --> 00:17:03,068
For real?

262
00:17:03,068 --> 00:17:04,068
Uh-huh!

263
00:17:04,068 --> 00:17:05,068
Let's load up!

264
00:17:05,068 --> 00:17:06,068
And go!

265
00:17:15,068 --> 00:17:17,068
Story goes, Vander Decken was hard up!

266
00:17:17,068 --> 00:17:21,068
The guy was totally head over heels for the mermaid princess of the Ryugu kingdom!

267
00:17:21,068 --> 00:17:23,068
He was so desperate, he sent love letters daily!

268
00:17:25,068 --> 00:17:26,068
How shockery!

269
00:17:26,068 --> 00:17:27,068
You know?

270
00:17:27,068 --> 00:17:28,068
Gave up letters!

271
00:17:28,068 --> 00:17:29,068
Started sending gifts instead!

272
00:17:29,068 --> 00:17:30,068
Then threats!

273
00:17:30,068 --> 00:17:31,068
Go to marry her!

274
00:17:31,068 --> 00:17:32,068
A bee!

275
00:17:32,068 --> 00:17:33,068
Feels great!

276
00:17:33,068 --> 00:17:34,068
Ringy Bums!

277
00:17:34,068 --> 00:17:35,068
Bums!

278
00:17:35,068 --> 00:17:36,068
Bums!

279
00:17:36,068 --> 00:17:37,068
Oh!

280
00:17:37,068 --> 00:17:38,068
Are you even listening to me?!

281
00:17:38,068 --> 00:17:39,068
Sure!

282
00:17:39,068 --> 00:17:40,068
Sorry about that!

283
00:17:40,068 --> 00:17:41,068
Ahem!

284
00:17:41,068 --> 00:17:45,068
Because his advances started to become so violent, the mermaid princess got scared!

285
00:17:45,068 --> 00:17:46,068
And so, of course!

286
00:17:46,068 --> 00:17:48,068
The stalker became a national concern!

287
00:17:48,068 --> 00:17:49,068
Yeah!

288
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:51,068
But that was just the beginning!

289
00:17:51,068 --> 00:17:53,068
Her father, King Neptune, got mad!

290
00:17:53,068 --> 00:17:58,068
Which led to him sending the three princes you saw earlier off to hunt Vander Decken!

291
00:17:58,068 --> 00:18:00,528
But even with the army, they can't find him.

292
00:18:00,888 --> 00:18:04,328
Oh, come on, Kami. You stole all my thunder.

293
00:18:04,508 --> 00:18:06,728
By the way, King Neptune's the god of the sea.

294
00:18:07,028 --> 00:18:08,568
Plus, he's in control of this country.

295
00:18:08,968 --> 00:18:12,648
If that's not enough responsibility, he has four children to take care of.

296
00:18:13,068 --> 00:18:14,688
The mermaid princess is the youngest,

297
00:18:15,168 --> 00:18:18,648
so obviously the three princes are the older kids in the royal family.

298
00:18:19,108 --> 00:18:20,848
Please, I got this.

299
00:18:21,188 --> 00:18:23,828
Great, but something still doesn't make sense.

300
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:25,908
Vanderdecken must be quite ancient.

301
00:18:25,908 --> 00:18:29,288
If he isn't a ghost, I imagine he's a few hundred years old.

302
00:18:29,568 --> 00:18:30,408
At least.

303
00:18:30,788 --> 00:18:33,728
Huh. You're right, that doesn't make sense.

304
00:18:33,948 --> 00:18:36,368
That is, unless you ignore the rumors.

305
00:18:37,148 --> 00:18:39,048
Now, there's no denying that he existed,

306
00:18:39,308 --> 00:18:42,688
but the truth of the matter is that the legendary sea captain Vanderdecken

307
00:18:42,688 --> 00:18:45,828
died sometime after he arrived here on Fishman Island

308
00:18:45,828 --> 00:18:47,568
and hasn't been heard from since.

309
00:18:48,408 --> 00:18:52,908
That said, the ship you say you saw probably was the Flying Dutchman, but...

310
00:18:52,908 --> 00:18:56,908
It's his descendant who's on board.

311
00:18:58,908 --> 00:18:59,348
He's...

312
00:18:59,348 --> 00:19:00,988
He's Vanderdecken the Ninth.

313
00:19:03,028 --> 00:19:05,228
Wow, that's a lot!

314
00:19:05,768 --> 00:19:09,188
Well, I have to say, it's a relief to find out he's not a ghost after all.

315
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:12,168
Believing we had come into contact with someone from the afterlife

316
00:19:12,168 --> 00:19:14,148
was making me contemplate my own mortality.

317
00:19:14,668 --> 00:19:17,448
And considering I'm a skeleton, I don't have much of that left.

318
00:19:17,448 --> 00:19:20,448
I just wanted to tell an exciting story.

319
00:19:20,688 --> 00:19:24,388
Man, I thought merfolk and fishmen all look the same,

320
00:19:24,468 --> 00:19:26,148
but the more I see, the less they do.

321
00:19:26,228 --> 00:19:27,808
Check out those old ones down there.

322
00:19:28,008 --> 00:19:29,908
Their fins are split like Granny Kokoro.

323
00:19:30,408 --> 00:19:32,108
See those babies? Right there.

324
00:19:32,508 --> 00:19:32,848
Huh?

325
00:19:33,248 --> 00:19:35,188
You'll notice the father is a fishman,

326
00:19:35,188 --> 00:19:37,108
but the children are a mix of both species.

327
00:19:37,848 --> 00:19:39,828
That's because when a mermaid and a fishman

328
00:19:39,828 --> 00:19:42,368
love each other very much and decide to get busy,

329
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:44,628
their kids can come out looking like either parent.

330
00:19:45,588 --> 00:19:46,048
Bam!

331
00:19:46,388 --> 00:19:48,168
Four possibilities for the happy family.

332
00:19:48,988 --> 00:19:51,148
Oh, that's why they all look different.

333
00:19:51,568 --> 00:19:52,428
So cool.

334
00:19:53,208 --> 00:19:55,268
All right, we finally made it to the highway.

335
00:19:59,528 --> 00:20:00,008
Whoa!

336
00:20:00,008 --> 00:20:01,428
This is fast!

337
00:20:02,548 --> 00:20:03,828
What's up with that place?

338
00:20:04,028 --> 00:20:04,908
Oh, nothing.

339
00:20:05,028 --> 00:20:05,988
It's a candy factory.

340
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:06,688
Really?

341
00:20:07,048 --> 00:20:08,888
Then why is there a pirate flag on it?

342
00:20:09,068 --> 00:20:09,688
Oh, that?

343
00:20:09,868 --> 00:20:11,188
That flag's everywhere here.

344
00:20:11,348 --> 00:20:12,548
By the entrance and the harbor.

345
00:20:12,888 --> 00:20:13,808
It's a big deal.

346
00:20:14,188 --> 00:20:15,488
And for good reason at that,

347
00:20:15,668 --> 00:20:17,768
it symbolizes that we're protected.

348
00:20:18,288 --> 00:20:20,868
You see, the flag belongs to a famous pirate

349
00:20:20,868 --> 00:20:22,988
named Charlotte Lin-Lin of the New World.

350
00:20:23,268 --> 00:20:25,028
But she's better known as Big Mom,

351
00:20:25,288 --> 00:20:26,528
one of the four emperors.

352
00:20:27,048 --> 00:20:28,628
Whoa, that's no joke.

353
00:20:28,628 --> 00:20:31,248
Back before the war in Marineford,

354
00:20:31,408 --> 00:20:32,928
Whitebeard was this island's guardian.

355
00:20:33,128 --> 00:20:33,968
But now that he's dead,

356
00:20:34,088 --> 00:20:35,628
someone else had to take his place.

357
00:20:35,828 --> 00:20:37,608
And that someone happened to be her.

358
00:20:38,428 --> 00:20:38,908
Okay.

359
00:20:40,028 --> 00:20:40,888
The thing is,

360
00:20:41,208 --> 00:20:42,888
she demands a whole ton of candy

361
00:20:42,888 --> 00:20:44,228
in exchange for her services.

362
00:20:44,968 --> 00:20:46,568
Hence the factory that you just saw.

363
00:20:47,108 --> 00:20:47,928
That's weird.

364
00:20:48,488 --> 00:20:50,308
This country wouldn't be able to survive

365
00:20:50,308 --> 00:20:52,528
without the protection of powerful people like her.

366
00:20:52,768 --> 00:20:54,388
After all, this is a dangerous place

367
00:20:54,388 --> 00:20:55,468
where pirates come and go.

368
00:20:55,468 --> 00:20:56,448
And more often than not,

369
00:20:56,528 --> 00:20:57,588
they aren't very friendly.

370
00:20:58,268 --> 00:20:59,088
Yeah, I guess.

371
00:20:59,328 --> 00:21:01,588
Plus, she's filling in where Whitebeard left off,

372
00:21:01,648 --> 00:21:02,468
so that's gotta mean

373
00:21:02,468 --> 00:21:03,808
she's a good person, doesn't it?

374
00:21:04,208 --> 00:21:05,608
Depends on how you look at it.

375
00:21:05,888 --> 00:21:07,288
Whitebeard never asked for anything

376
00:21:07,288 --> 00:21:08,528
in return for his protection.

377
00:21:08,968 --> 00:21:10,048
Big Mom, on the other hand,

378
00:21:10,108 --> 00:21:11,168
treats it like a business

379
00:21:11,168 --> 00:21:12,188
rather than a charity.

380
00:21:12,388 --> 00:21:13,568
Still, that's cool.

381
00:21:14,088 --> 00:21:14,768
An emperor.

382
00:21:15,388 --> 00:21:16,068
Like shakes.

383
00:21:16,408 --> 00:21:16,848
Crazy.

384
00:21:17,148 --> 00:21:18,148
Hope they get to meet her.

385
00:21:18,808 --> 00:21:19,588
Eyes forward.

386
00:21:20,288 --> 00:21:22,448
This is where all the celebrity types live.

387
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:23,948
Fisperly Hills!

388
00:21:25,448 --> 00:21:27,068
That tall building right in front

389
00:21:27,068 --> 00:21:28,088
is Papa Goose's house,

390
00:21:28,168 --> 00:21:28,968
where we're going.

391
00:21:29,768 --> 00:21:30,508
All that?

392
00:21:31,008 --> 00:21:32,428
For one starfish?

393
00:21:32,428 --> 00:21:40,008
We have to do something.

394
00:21:40,608 --> 00:21:42,208
We can't let this happen.

395
00:21:42,488 --> 00:21:43,628
That's Madam Charlie,

396
00:21:43,988 --> 00:21:44,728
from the cafe.

397
00:21:45,228 --> 00:21:46,188
What's the matter?

398
00:21:46,508 --> 00:21:47,848
Please, please tell us.

399
00:21:47,988 --> 00:21:48,608
What's wrong?

400
00:21:48,788 --> 00:21:49,648
Why are you upset?

401
00:21:50,008 --> 00:21:51,388
Something must be done.

402
00:21:51,628 --> 00:21:52,928
Now before it's too late.

403
00:21:53,668 --> 00:21:54,228
Sure.

404
00:21:54,528 --> 00:21:55,408
What do we do?

405
00:21:55,408 --> 00:21:58,628
Find him!

406
00:21:59,348 --> 00:22:00,988
The pirate boy in a straw hat!

407
00:22:01,148 --> 00:22:01,928
It's an emergency!

408
00:22:04,108 --> 00:22:05,768
He must leave the country!

409
00:22:06,048 --> 00:22:06,448
Now!

410
00:22:06,708 --> 00:22:07,648
There's no time!

411
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,708
Wait, you're having a premonition?

412
00:22:09,968 --> 00:22:11,628
I swore I wouldn't use this power,

413
00:22:12,048 --> 00:22:13,408
but something about that boy

414
00:22:13,408 --> 00:22:14,248
felt off to me.

415
00:22:14,888 --> 00:22:15,248
I...

416
00:22:15,248 --> 00:22:16,848
I had no choice

417
00:22:16,848 --> 00:22:18,228
but to look into the future!

418
00:22:19,968 --> 00:22:21,128
What's going to happen?

419
00:22:21,528 --> 00:22:23,168
Tell us, what did you see?

420
00:22:23,388 --> 00:22:24,548
We have to know!

421
00:22:24,548 --> 00:22:25,748
Charlie!

422
00:22:26,288 --> 00:22:27,108
Tell us!

423
00:22:27,368 --> 00:22:27,888
Madam!

424
00:22:28,328 --> 00:22:28,848
Please!

425
00:22:30,128 --> 00:22:31,548
I hope I'm wrong

426
00:22:31,548 --> 00:22:32,568
and that

427
00:22:32,568 --> 00:22:33,728
it won't happen.

428
00:22:49,608 --> 00:22:51,248
I saw him clearly,

429
00:22:51,568 --> 00:22:52,768
surrounded by flames.

430
00:22:54,548 --> 00:22:56,648
Because of Straw Hat Luffy,

431
00:22:57,568 --> 00:22:58,848
Fishman Island,

432
00:22:59,388 --> 00:23:00,548
our country will be...

433
00:23:02,148 --> 00:23:04,048
destroyed!

434
00:23:04,048 --> 00:23:10,468
Beneath its dazzling exterior,

435
00:23:10,688 --> 00:23:12,728
Fishman Island hides a dark history.

436
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:14,568
Harboring an age-old grudge,

437
00:23:14,688 --> 00:23:16,888
the residents of the island prepare to take action.

438
00:23:18,028 --> 00:23:21,708
Meanwhile, Luffy and friends cause a commotion at Papagoo's shop

439
00:23:21,708 --> 00:23:24,608
and have an unexpected encounter with Neptune,

440
00:23:25,268 --> 00:23:26,448
King of Fishman Island.

441
00:23:26,448 --> 00:23:27,848
On the next,

442
00:23:28,008 --> 00:23:28,608
One Piece,

443
00:23:28,928 --> 00:23:30,528
the King of the Fishman Island,

444
00:23:30,788 --> 00:23:31,128
Neptune,

445
00:23:31,328 --> 00:23:32,288
the God of the Sea.

446
00:23:32,848 --> 00:23:34,948
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

